  "narrative": "The new validation decisively strengthens H12 and disposes of the unresolved H4. For H12, SMARCA4-loss versus dependency_SMARCA2, discovery R12 was +0.782 [0.761, 0.802], signed to the hypothesis that SMARCA4-loss cells have stronger, more negative SMARCA2 dependency. Independent validation R39 was +0.805 [0.775, 0.836] under the stricter validation-adjusted interval. The lower bounds are far above any reasonable approximate 10% effect benchmark on the SMARCA2 score scale, and discovery and validation magnitudes are highly consistent. Therefore H12 is accepted as an independently replicated dataset-specific association, not as a causal or clinical claim. The previously accepted within-context confirmations H26 adenocarcinoma, H36 Ky library, and H40 adherent culture are now treated as completed robustness checks and closed. The borderline Ky interaction H29 also is closed as an investigation line because the central effect is validated and very large in Ky itself, although the interaction estimate remains statistically imprecise and unresolved in a strict sense.\n\nFor H4, EGFR amplification versus dependency_EGFR, the response-deadline validation is negative for the registered hypothesis. Discovery R4 was only weakly positive in the claimed stronger-dependency direction, +0.029 [0.001, 0.057], and validation R13 was -0.013 [-0.059, 0.033], crossing zero and pointing in the opposite signed direction. There is no stable evidence for a clinically meaningful EGFR-amplification association with EGFR dependency. I therefore reject H4 and close it. This is an important negative control against overinterpreting small near-threshold discovery estimates.\n\nThe current supported core findings are: MSI-high cells show stronger WRN dependency, replicated in H11 and context-supported in H25/H37/H39; SMARCA4-loss cells show stronger SMARCA2 dependency, now replicated in H12 and context-supported in H26/H36/H40; KEAP1-loss cells show weaker NFE2L2 dependency in H13, H27, H38, and H41, but this major association has not yet received independent validation; and TP53-loss cells show weaker USP7 dependency in H48, with a very large discovery estimate +0.804 [0.783, 0.825], also not yet validated. Negative or rejected findings include KRAS mutation on BRAF dependency, BRAF V600E on BRAF dependency, EGFR amplification on STAT3 and EGFR dependency, the original KEAP1-loss stronger-NFE2L2 direction, MYC amplification on POLR2A dependency, the SMARCA4-loss lineage-subtype interaction, the MSI-high Ky-library interaction, and KRAS mutation on RIT1 dependency. Unresolved low-priority uncertainty remains for small direct EGFR, ERBB2, TP53-MDM2, MYC-USP7, marker-modifier, and some interaction contrasts.\n\nThe most informative next analyses are the TP53-loss/USP7 context tests H51-H54, followed by marker-modifier tests for the accepted effects H17-H23, and broad KIF18A tests H55-H56. If TP53-loss/USP7 remains large and consistent across adenocarcinoma, Ky, adherent, and MTAP-loss contexts, H48 should become the next independent validation target; if it is context-specific or attenuated, investigate the context before validation. H13 remains a later validation candidate. All conclusions remain associations in this supplied dataset and supplied validation splits, not causal effects or guaranteed generalizable findings.",
  "research_notes": "Core validated dataset-specific associations: H11 MSI-high stronger WRN dependency; H12 SMARCA4-loss stronger SMARCA2 dependency. H4 EGFR amplification/EGFR dependency rejected due failed validation and weak discovery. Strong but unvalidated: H13 KEAP1-loss weaker NFE2L2 dependency; H48 TP53-loss weaker USP7 dependency, very large but needs context tests and validation. Context claims closed as robustness checks: H25/H37/H39 for WRN; H26/H36/H40 for SMARCA2. H29 unresolved but closed as interaction line because central H12 validated and H36 direct Ky effect huge. Next analyze priorities: H51-H54 USP7/TP53 context tests; then marker modifiers H17-H23 for accepted effects; new broad KIF18A tests H55-H56. If H48 is consistent, request validation H48 next; then H13. Continue to avoid causal/generalizability claims and account for correlated genomic alterations and multiple testing."
